From 6ee538d12642f7865574f5b1c395053240657772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: odapplications <27908286+odapplications@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:53:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: refuse to emit exponentially backtracking regexes
 (CVE-2026-112366)

Check every regex parse() builds for exponential degree of ambiguity
(Weber-Seidl test on its Glushkov automaton, adapted to a backtracking
engine). If it is exponentially ambiguous, match the pattern as literal
text, the same fallback maxExtglobRecursion already uses. Invalid
generated regexes are left alone, since makeRe() already turns them
into one that matches nothing.

The analyzer lives in the new, dependency-free lib/ambiguity.js; parse()
only gains the final check. Opt out with maxExtglobRecursion: false.

Refs #234, GHSA-fc5q-39xc-vjpf.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
